---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NOSTR_URL, SITE_NAME } from '../../consts.ts';
---
<Base locale="en" title={`About · ${SITE_NAME}`} description="How Bitcoin Security Watcher selects and publishes security alerts." counterpartUrl="/about/">
  <article class="prose" style="padding-top: 32px">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Bitcoin Security Watcher tracks security issues that could cost bitcoiners money or put them at risk: bugs, vulnerabilities, personal data leaks, compromised software packages and more.</p>
    <h2>What counts as critical?</h2>
    <p>We publish announcements that call for action or awareness today. Audience labels help readers tell whether an alert concerns them.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>Alerts are published automatically. Code collects and deduplicates source reports; a language model assesses the signals. Mistakes can reach the public feed. Human review around the clock is not sustainable for our nonprofit project, so we use automation to keep alerts timely.</p>
    <p><a href="/en/sources">See the projects and channels we monitor</a>.</p>
    <h2>Where to read</h2>
    <p>Announcements are published on <a href="/en/feed">this website</a> and distributed via <a href="/en/rss.xml">RSS</a> and posted on the <a href={NOSTR_URL} rel="noopener">21ideas Nostr profile</a>.</p>
    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>Security Watcher is a nonprofit 21ideas project. Server infrastructure, site maintenance, and model calls need funding. <a href="/en/support">Support the project</a> if you find it useful.</p>
    <p class="note">A <a href="https://21ideas.org" rel="noopener">21ideas</a> project. The <a href="https://github.com/21ideas-org/sec-web" rel="noopener">site source code</a> is public.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
